  "@aboutDataCountUnavailable": {
    "description": "A count that could not be computed, and NOT a zero. The distinction is the whole reason the three figures are evidence for B31: a zero says 'you have none' and a dash says 'we could not look', and a reader who took the first for the second would re-download a library they still have."
  },
  "@aboutDataE11": {
    "description": "E11, in full and unhedged. This app has no backup (ADR-010), so the disclosure belongs on the page that shows what would be lost — and it names the exact operation that does NOT lose it, because a disclosure that only lists risks reads as an apology."
  },
